;; tokens * 10^12 / elapsed_ns, executed in the `kotoba.kir` oracle against
;; the answers the RETIRED C `aiueos_inference_milli_tokens_per_second` gave
;; at aiueos 352c385 (ADR-0219). Arguments and results are the uint64_t bit
;; patterns as signed words: UNMEASURED (UINT64_MAX) is -1 on both sides.
;;
;; ⚠ The oracle host reads EDN integers as doubles, so two vectors whose
;; expected value lies above 2^53 (`:max-tokens-one-ns`, `:max-tokens-three-ns`)
;; are compared to ~11 significant digits here and cannot pin the low bits.
;; Those two, and every other vector below, were ALSO executed as native
;; aarch64 code through amu's kexe loader with the exact answer (measured
;; 2026-09-16, recorded in ADR-0219); the oracle floor for them is the
;; magnitude, the native run is the value.
